;; std/combinator.blsp — the less common functions over functions (ADR-506).
;;
;; Defined in the prelude under these qualified names; where a function is defined says
;; nothing about what it is called. This file declares the module they belong to and
;; documents the surface. `identity`, `partial` and `comp` stay bare: they are the language's
;; own vocabulary. `(:use combinator)` brings these back bare.

(defmodule combinator
  "Adapters that build a function from functions or values.

    ((combinator/complement nil?) 1)         ;=> true
    ((combinator/constantly :x) 1 2)         ;=> :x
    ((combinator/juxt first last) [1 2 3])   ;=> [1 3]
    ((combinator/fnil inc 0) nil)            ;=> 1

To remember a function's answers, define it with `memo/defmemo` (ADR-522).")
